WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.055
When a shared notebook changes, numbered history helps you see

2
00:00:04.055 --> 00:00:06.308
what happened without erasing earlier pages.

3
00:00:06.308 --> 00:00:10.063
Software needs something similar. State is the information a program

4
00:00:10.063 --> 00:00:13.817
currently holds. Frame Chains organizes that changing state as records

5
00:00:13.817 --> 00:00:16.445
that can be checked, linked, and replayed.

6
00:00:16.445 --> 00:00:18.698
A convincing screen is not enough:

7
00:00:18.698 --> 00:00:22.452
we need to know which change was allowed and which

8
00:00:22.452 --> 00:00:24.705
accepted state can still be trusted.

9
00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:29.336
A frame is one recorded event or state description, not

10
00:00:29.336 --> 00:00:31.135
a picture in a movie.

11
00:00:31.135 --> 00:00:34.373
A chain links those records into a checkable history.

12
00:00:34.373 --> 00:00:37.251
A hash is a fingerprint computed from data:

13
00:00:37.251 --> 00:00:40.848
it can reveal changed bytes, but cannot by itself prove

14
00:00:40.848 --> 00:00:42.647
a story or a cause.

15
00:00:42.647 --> 00:00:45.525
A verifier checks the recorded data and rules.

16
00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:49.122
The accepted head is the latest record that passed those

17
00:00:49.122 --> 00:00:49.482
checks.

18
00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.914
These ten worlds are proof models:

19
00:00:52.914 --> 00:00:56.911
deliberately simplified programs that test specific rules, not real colonies

20
00:00:56.911 --> 00:01:00.908
or conscious digital people. A branch is a separate continuation

21
00:01:00.908 --> 00:01:04.905
of history. A projection or lens is a different interface

22
00:01:04.905 --> 00:01:08.902
onto the same history. A live replay is a running

23
00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.300
application you can pause and operate.

24
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.297
Watch a valid change succeed, a bad change get refused,

25
00:01:15.297 --> 00:01:17.695
and the accepted state remain intact.

26
00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.720
An interactive proof

27
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:20.750
can still confuse

28
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:21.860
a newcomer.

29
00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:22.070
So,

30
00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.210
RAPP Vision pairs

31
00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:24.470
every live replay

32
00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:24.790
with

33
00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.100
a real film.

34
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.550
Understand it first,

35
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:28.110
then take

36
00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.040
the controls.

37
00:01:29.241 --> 00:01:30.801
One identity crosses

38
00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:31.761
devices,

39
00:01:31.771 --> 00:01:32.961
branches offline,

40
00:01:32.961 --> 00:01:34.481
and returns.

41
00:01:34.481 --> 00:01:34.921
The film

42
00:01:34.921 --> 00:01:36.361
shows the journey.

43
00:01:36.361 --> 00:01:37.521
The verifier rejects

44
00:01:37.521 --> 00:01:39.691
the counterfeit without moving

45
00:01:39.691 --> 00:01:40.484
the accepted

46
00:01:40.484 --> 00:01:40.671
On Mars,

47
00:01:40.671 --> 00:01:41.114
head.

48
00:01:41.114 --> 00:01:41.254
a

49
00:01:41.454 --> 00:01:44.494
correctly-hashed repair still fails.

50
00:01:44.494 --> 00:01:44.994
The chain

51
00:01:44.994 --> 00:01:45.254
proves

52
00:01:45.454 --> 00:01:46.694
exactly which three

53
00:01:46.694 --> 00:01:48.034
systems were authorized

54
00:01:48.494 --> 00:01:49.244
and preserves

55
00:01:49.454 --> 00:01:50.534
the colony's last

56
00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:51.139
good state.

57
00:01:51.139 --> 00:01:52.459
one history becomes

58
00:01:52.459 --> 00:01:53.999
five interfaces.

59
00:01:53.999 --> 00:01:55.619
When command lies,

60
00:01:55.619 --> 00:01:57.049
four honest projections

61
00:01:57.049 --> 00:01:58.259
still agree,

62
00:01:58.259 --> 00:01:58.629
and the

63
00:01:58.629 --> 00:02:00.009
broken lens isolates

64
00:02:00.009 --> 00:02:00.699
itself.

65
00:02:00.699 --> 00:02:01.979
The detective accepts

66
00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:02.419
only a

67
00:02:02.419 --> 00:02:03.129
theory backed

68
00:02:03.219 --> 00:02:04.569
by exact earlier

69
00:02:04.569 --> 00:02:05.539
causes.

70
00:02:05.539 --> 00:02:07.289
Forge one plausible

71
00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:08.669
clue and cryptography

72
00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:10.089
stays green while

73
00:02:10.089 --> 00:02:11.461
causality turns red.

74
00:02:11.461 --> 00:02:12.481
Six agents build

75
00:02:12.481 --> 00:02:13.631
one station without

76
00:02:13.711 --> 00:02:15.541
